      "mergedPostDetails": "VRC Build : 1093\nSDK Version : UNU 2021.05.07.14.27\nWhen setting up a NavMesh agent, I discovered an issue where inside the VRC client, the agent ignores the cost of a specific area, while in the editor it works just fine.\nTo recreate, upload a test world with an AI that has an area with a cost much higher than a short roundabout path.\nIn this test world, the blue area has a cost of 50, while the surrounding area has a cost of 1. \nTest world | https://vrch.at/brou-pettijupiter-8383e",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1093] NavMesh Agents ignore NavMesh area cost when calculating path",
